X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
DESCRIPTION:National Whiskey Sour Day is observed on August 25 across the
  United States. A whiskey sour is a classic cocktail containing whiskey (
 often bourbon), lemon juice, and sugar. The oldest written recipe appears
  in Jerry Thomas's The Bartender's Guide, published in 1862. https://nati
 onaltoday.com/national-whiskey-sour-day/
LOCATION:Pastafarian Holy Day
URL:https://www.pastafariancalendar.com/whiskey-sour-day-2024-08-25?utm_s
 ource=ical&utm_medium=ical
