DTSTAMP:20260811T203849Z
CATEGORIES:Holiday
SUMMARY:🪢 Knot Day 🪢
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20251009
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20251010
UID:pastafarian-2025-10-09
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
DESCRIPTION:The International Guild of Knot Tyers created World Knot Tyin
 g Day to celebrate and remember the author Clifford W Ashley, who wrote a
 nd illustrated The Ashley Book of Knots. Participants were asked to tie t
 heir favorite knot and also learn a new knot. Maybe also teach someone ho
 w to tie a knot? Even teaching someone to tie their shoelaces was suffici
 ent. When the knots were tied, participants were encouraged to post a pho
 to of their knot on their favorite social media site with the hashtag #Wo
 rldKnotTyingDay. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Guild_of_Kno
 t_Tyers#World_Knot_Tying_Day
LOCATION:Pastafarian Holy Day
URL:https://www.pastafariancalendar.com/knot-day-2025-10-09?utm_source=ic
 al&utm_medium=ical
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:The International Guild of Knot Tyers created World Knot Tyin
 g Day to celebrate and remember the author Clifford W Ashley, who wrote a
 nd illustrated The Ashley Book of Knots. Participants were asked to tie t
 heir favorite knot and also learn a new knot. Maybe also teach someone ho
 w to tie a knot? Even teaching someone to tie their shoelaces was suffici
 ent. When the knots were tied, participants were encouraged to post a pho
 to of their knot on their favorite social media site with the hashtag #Wo
 rldKnotTyingDay. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Guild_of_Kno
 t_Tyers#World_Knot_Tying_Day
